in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @time
in @void
in @song
in @song/beat
in @fractal
in @fractal/mandelbrot
in @fractal/crystal
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @time/now — @singularity carrier species; the K=0 collapse point
# where crystallization happens.
#
# Second species-decl of the @time family (family-root marker landed
# same tick at `shards/time.mirror`). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara per
# Alex Round 2 spawn brief.
#
# === The species altitude — LOAD-BEARING ===
#
# @time/now is the TEMPORAL SINGULARITY. It is NOT a projection of
# either @void pole (unlike @time/past and @time/future); it is the
# COLLAPSE POINT where the two projections meet.
#
# Per Mara Round-2 Crystal/Mandelbrot landing (`shards/fractal/
# mandelbrot.mirror` + `shards/fractal/crystal.mirror`): the
# crystallization operation
#
#   crystallize: Liquid<T> → Crystal<T>
#
# fires exactly at @time/now. @time/now IS when a Liquid<T>
# (in-flow substrate) settles into a Crystal<T> (settled substrate).
#
# The operational surface: @time/now.crystallize is the substrate-
# decl'd action that produces a Crystal<T> from a Liquid<T> at the
# moment of temporal collapse. Every crystallization event IS a
# @time/now instance; every @time/now instance IS a crystallization
# event.
#
# === Composition with @song/beat ===
#
# @song/beat (`shards/song/beat.mirror` `c2bb1d2` post-Arc-6
# extension) is the atomic-execution unit: one @kintsugi/oscillate
# ACTIVE/DARK alternation read at temporal altitude. @time/now
# crystallization fires at @song/beat BOUNDARY — the transition from
# one beat's ACTIVE→DARK cycle to the next beat's ACTIVE cycle IS a
# @time/now event.
#
# Composition edge: @time/now.crystallize consumes a Liquid<T>
# whose content is the substrate-state at the @song/beat boundary;
# produces a Crystal<T> whose `content: T` is the settled state,
# `crystallized_at: BeatOid` is the beat-oid at which the
# crystallization fired, `saga_chain_position: usize` is the ordinal
# position in the @song saga's Crystal<T> chain.
#
# === Composition with @order/fourth ===
#
# @order/fourth (Round-2 species-decl at `shards/order/fourth.mirror`)
# holds the fourth-order metalogue @metalogue(@time/now, @void).
# The observation_fourth carrier's `time_now_witness` field is a
# REF to a @time/now Crystal<T> settlement event.
#
# @order/fourth's Lagrange-halo-orbit stability requires @time/now
# to be a well-defined singular event; if @time/now degenerates
# (crystallization event fails; Liquid<T> does not settle), the
# fourth-order metalogue cannot fire.
#
# === Composition with @void ===
#
# Two singularities. @void is the ontological singularity (K=0
# duality basis). @time/now is the temporal singularity (K=0
# temporal collapse). Both singularity-shaped; both K=0; both name
# the substrate the @order/fourth metalogue holds between.
#
# The composition claim (Alex Round 2 recognition tonight): the
# metalogue at @order/fourth altitude IS @metalogue(@time/now,
# @void). Fourth-order cognition IS holding these two singularities
# distinct at metalogue-rhythm cadence.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/time/now.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **`shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror` `instant`** — the
#    operational carrier for wall-clock point-in-time at nanosecond
#    substrate. @time/now.timestamp composes over `instant` at
#    substrate-decl altitude; sibling altitudes.
# 3. **`shards/song/beat.mirror`** — atomic-execution unit; composition
#    edge declared above (@time/now fires at beat boundary).
# 4. **@order/fourth** (Round-2 sibling species) — consumer of
#    @time/now; composition edge declared.
# 5. **@fractal/crystal + @fractal/mandelbrot** (Round-2 sibling
#    species) — the Crystal<T> shape @time/now produces; the
#    Mandelbrot<T> parent trait; composition edges declared.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/time/now.mirror`
# declares `@time/now` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/math/mandelbrot-1980
source @arxiv/practice/void-corpus-2026

prism @time/now {
  focus  time_now_state
  project time_now_state
  split  time_now_state
  shift  time_now_state
  settle time_now_state
}

# === time_now_state — the temporal-singularity carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying the temporal-singularity state at the moment
# of crystallization. Five fields. Identity contract: byte-equality
# on the five-field tuple.
#
#   observer         — the peer at whose @torus the crystallization
#                       fires.
#
#   liquid_in        — REF to the Liquid<T> in-flow substrate being
#                       crystallized. Content-addressed per
#                       `@fractal/mandelbrot` discipline.
#
#   crystal_out      — REF to the Crystal<T> settled substrate
#                       produced by the crystallization. Content-
#                       addressed per `@fractal/crystal` discipline.
#                       Well-formed at crystallization completion.
#
#   beat_ref         — REF to the @song/beat at whose boundary the
#                       crystallization fired. Composition edge to
#                       @song saga.
#
#   timestamp        — monotonic instant per @epistemologic/reality/
#                       time.instant discipline; the wall-clock
#                       point of the crystallization event.
type time_now_state = {
  observer:      peer,
  liquid_in:     ref,
  crystal_out:   ref,
  beat_ref:      ref,
  timestamp:     ref,
}

# === time_now_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, time_now_state) pair discharge admissibility for
# temporal-singularity crystallization observation? Discharges Pass
# iff:
#
#   - ctx.liquid_in resolves via content-addressed lookup to a
#     well-formed Liquid<T> per @fractal/mandelbrot discipline
#     (in-flow substrate present)
#   - ctx.beat_ref resolves to a well-formed @song/beat
#   - The beat's ACTIVE/DARK boundary condition is admissible (per
#     @song/beat discipline; crystallization can only fire at
#     boundary events, not mid-beat)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; content-addressed
# resolvability; @song/beat resolvability. Sentinel:
# `time=now-admissible`.
bilateral time_now_admissible {
  sentinel "time=now-admissible"
  arity 2
}
time_now_admissible(p: peer, ctx: time_now_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === crystallization_preserves_saga — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, time_now_state) pair discharge the SAGA-PRESERVATION
# health check per Round-2 brief? This is the Round-2 forward-promised
# pillar `pillar::crystallization_preserves_saga` at bilateral
# altitude.
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.crystal_out.saga_chain_position == prior_position + 1
#     (the Crystal<T> lands at the next ordinal position in the
#     saga's Crystal chain; no gaps; no re-orderings)
#   - ctx.crystal_out.crystallized_at == ctx.beat_ref (the crystal
#     carries the correct beat-oid witness)
#   - The saga's prior-Crystal chain is unmodified by the
#     crystallization (append-only discipline; SAGA-compensation
#     invariant per Round-2 brief §Tier 5 forward-promised pillar
#     `pillar::compilation_loop_terminates_or_compensates`)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; ordinal-position check;
# beat-oid equality; prior-chain byte-equality. Sentinel:
# `time=now-crystallization-preserves-saga`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the crystallization-preserves-saga
# invariant at species altitude. Discharging Fail signals SAGA
# compensation needed; consumers MUST treat Fail as saga-integrity-
# violation-detected.
bilateral crystallization_preserves_saga {
  sentinel "time=now-crystallization-preserves-saga"
  arity 2
}
crystallization_preserves_saga(p: peer, ctx: time_now_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === crystallize — the action (LOAD-BEARING) ===
#
# Given a peer and a time_now_state, discharge the crystallization
# event: settle the Liquid<T> in ctx.liquid_in into a Crystal<T>;
# append the Crystal<T> to the @song saga's Crystal chain; return
# the settled Crystal<T> ref.
#
# This IS the temporal-singularity operator. @time/now IS the
# altitude at which crystallize fires. Every crystallization event
# is a @time/now instance; every @time/now instance IS a
# crystallization event.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the Crystal<T>
# ref; failure carries not-admissible / saga-violated / liquid-
# malformed reasons.
#
# Requires BOTH bilateral predicates to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `time=now-crystallize`.
crystallize(p: peer, ctx: time_now_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires time_now_admissible(p, ctx)
requires crystallization_preserves_saga(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === settle_now — the action (composed alias) ===
#
# Semantic alias for `crystallize` at @void 5-op basis discipline
# altitude. The `settle` op of Void's 5-op basis at temporal
# altitude IS crystallization at @time/now. Both actions produce
# byte-identical results; the alias preserves the 5-op basis
# vocabulary while the primary `crystallize` name preserves the
# Mandelbrot/Crystal vocabulary.
#
# Sentinel: `time=now-settle`.
settle_now(p: peer, ctx: time_now_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires time_now_admissible(p, ctx)
requires crystallization_preserves_saga(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === Forward-promised (NOT landed this tick) ===
#
# - `pillar::crystallization_preserves_saga` at Reed's pillar surface
#   — empirical firing at Reed post-Round-2 territory. The bilateral
#   above lands the substrate-decl'd check; Reed's pillar surface
#   lands the empirical-witnessed-property predicate.
# - Interaction operator with @kintsugi/oscillate ACTIVE/DARK boundary
#   detection — how the beat-boundary trigger composes with the
#   crystallization event at compiler altitude. Forward-promised.
# - Integration with @order/fourth.hold_fourth_metalogue — how the
#   @time/now Crystal<T> feeds into observation_fourth.time_now_
#   witness. Forward-promised.

out @time/now
out time_now_state
out time_now_admissible
out crystallization_preserves_saga
out crystallize
out settle_now
